music BGM14.mp3
text The warm spring sunlight shines down on me.
text A refreshing breeze blows past.
text I have plenty of leeway to make it to school on time.
text @[Tomoya]
text If I keep walking at this pace, there's no way I'll be late.
text It's not that I believe Fujibayashi's fortune from yesterday.
text However, just to be safe, I am walking to school earlier than usual.
text But then again, to other students this might already count as being a bit late.
text There aren't that many people wearing school uniforms along this road anymore.
text In any case, it's still early enough for me to get to school on time.
text Now according to Fujibayashi's fortune, there should be an old lady having trouble crossing the street.
text And I'll be late if I were to help her...
text @[Tomoya]
text To begin with, there isn't an old lady at the crosswal─
text I glance just beyond the white lines, painted like a ladder on the asphalt.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...I don't like this...
text Where I am looking, there's an old lady holding onto a utility pole with her hip stooped.
text She keeps glancing left and right.
text No matter how I look at it, something is wrong.
text All the other students feign ignorance and simply walk past her.
text And... our eyes meet.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text @[Old Lady]
text ...
text Perhaps it's just me, but it feels like she's staring at me.
text It almost feels like she's silently saying, "You can't even lend a helping hand when others are in trouble?"
text If I give in to those eyes, will Fujibayashi's fortune come true?
choice Talk to the old lady|Just keep walking
setvar intF[1089] = selected
sound 02.aac
setvar intF[1089] - 1
if intF[1089] == 0
	goto s1
fi
goto 2
label s1
text @[Tomoya]
text *Sigh*
text I would really love to pretend I didn't see her, but I can't just leave her be when she's looking at me like that.
text I guess I am more of a busybody than I thought.
text I let out a sigh and walk to the crosswalk.
text @[Tomoya]
text Hey, ma'a─
sound 8EZ.aac
text @[Old Lady]
text Yaaaahh!
text She suddenly screams at me.
text @[Tomoya]
text You're trying to cross the street, aren't...
sound 8F0.aac
text @[Old Lady]
text Yaaaahh!
text She keeps yelling at me as she steps backward.
text @[Tomoya]
text Like I was saying, are you...
sound 8F1.aac
text @[Old Lady]
text Yaaaahh!
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
sound 8F2.aac
text @[Old Lady]
text Yaaaahh!
text @[Tomoya]
text Say something that makes sense!
sound 8F3.aac
text @[Old Lady]
text Eek! What a scary kid... picking on the elderly.
text Fine, you old hag...
sound 8F4.aac
text @[Female Student]
text Hey, look! That guy's mugging that old lady!
sound 8F5.aac
text @[Female Student]
text Oh, it's that third-year delinquent.
sound 8F6.aac
text @[Male Student]
text Yeah, you're right. He does look like a bad person.
sound 8F7.aac
text @[Male Student]
text Somebody call for help! He's going to beat the old lady to death!
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text Well, that's strange. For once I am trying to do something nice, and everyone here is vilifying me for it.
text As my attention shifts to the rubberneckers, the old lady suddenly moves.
text She takes a step back, straightens her bent back, and quickly reaches for the ground.
text Right where her foot was...
text There's something shining... a 500 yen coin?
text In the blink of an eye she snatches it off the ground and runs off at a speed that would put younger people to shame.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...Hey...?
text Don't tell me... She was looking around because she was waiting to pick up the 500 yen coin?
text And did she yell at me so that I wouldn't take her 500 yen...?
sound 8F8.aac
text @[Female Student]
text Oh thank goodness. She managed to get away.
sound 8F9.aac
text @[Female Student]
text I really thought she was going to be beaten to death!
sound 8FA.aac
text @[Male Student]
text Hah, that guy's surprisingly slow.
sound 8FB.aac
text @[Male Student]
text I guess he's not that tough after all.
text @[Tomoya]
text What the hell are you staring at, huh?!
sound 8FC.aac
text @[Female Student]
text Aahh! He's coming this way!
sound 8FD.aac
text @[Male Student]
text Crap! Run!
text The onlookers scramble away like baby spiders.
text Geez... what's with this morning?
text I'll be thanked and get some money for my trouble?
text Fujibayashi's fortune was a sham!
text Hell, I'm an idiot for believing it for even a second!
goto 3
label 2
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text Nah... I'll just walk past her.
text I'd rather not be late like Fujibayashi said, all for some old hag that I don't know.
text To make it sound cool, I'm standing up against fate.
text I'll defy the future that her fortune foretold.
text I look away as I walk past the lady.
text I can feel her eyesight pricking my skin.
text Well granny, if you want to blame someone, blame my class president.
text You have lived for a long time and so you should know the transience of life very well.
text In any case, I walk past her without incident.
sound 8FE.aac
text @[Female Student]
text Excuse me ma'am, are you trying to cross the street?
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text Right after I walk past the old lady, a female student talks to her.
text It makes me feel a little guilty.
sound 8FF.aac
text @[Old Lady]
text Yaaaahh!
sound 8FG.aac
text @[Female Student]
text Aah?! What's going on? Was I mistaken?!
sound 8FH.aac
text @[Old Lady]
text Yaaaahh!
text For some reason the lady starts threatening the girl.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...Thank goodness I didn't talk to her.
text At any rate, Fujibayashi's fortune turned out to be wrong... I guess.
